{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"head -35 claims_grounding.json; sed -n '38,49p' paper.tex; sed -n '1,22p' build_artifacts.py; sed -n '45,60p' build_artifacts.py; sed -n '180,220p' paper_strategy.json; sed -n '1,40p' .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py; head -35 scientific-evidence/verification-report.json; sed -n '1,80p' .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Complete seed-table and machine-readable result row, seed 1009, condition S64K1: {\\\"control_failure_rate\\\": 0.0, \\\"coverage\\\": 0.951904296875, \\\"decision_reversal_rate\\\": 0.0, \\\"failure_rate\\\": 0.0, \\\"fixed_prompt_mse\\\": 0.003808543682098389, \\\"full_budget_naive_mse\\\": 0.003808543682098389, \\\"honest_half_mse\\\": 0.007740268707275391, \\\"interval_width\\\": 0.31687861103992715, \\\"random_prompt_mse\\\": 0.003808543682098389, \\\"report_bias\\\": -0.00043487548828125, \\\"report_mse\\\": 0.007617864608764648, \\\"reuse_mse\\\": 0.007430610656738282, \\\"selected_accuracy\\\": 0.5, \\\"signed_optimism\\\": 0.00146484375}.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"evidence_refs\": [\n        \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/solution/cases/0\",\n        \"analysis/condition_results.csv\",\n        \"tables/seed_results.tex\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Complete seed-table and machine-readable result row, seed 1009, condition S64K16: {\\\"control_failure_rate\\\": 0.0, \\\"coverage\\\": 0.959716796875, \\\"decision_reversal_rate\\\": 0.000732421875, \\\"failure_rate\\\": 0.0, \\\"fixed_prompt_mse\\\": 0.003661665916442871, \\\"full_budget_naive_mse\\\": 0.005447328111860487, \\\"honest_half_mse\\\": 0.006518946880764431, \\\"interval_width\\\": 0.29644363988131484, \\\"random_prompt_mse\\\": 0.0032765861405266656, \\\"report_bias\\\": -0.0010075887044270974, \\\"report_mse\\\": 0.006069530275132921, \\\"reuse_mse\\\": 0.011940063264634874, \\\"selected_accuracy\\\": 0.6842122395833333, \\\"signed_optimism\\\": 0.0725550333658854}.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"evidence_refs\": [\n        \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/solution/cases/1\",\n        \"analysis/condition_results.csv\",\n        \"tables/seed_results.tex\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Complete seed-table and machine-readable result row, seed 1009, condition S256K1: {\\\"control_failure_rate\\\": 0.0, \\\"coverage\\\": 0.95361328125, \\\"decision_reversal_rate\\\": 0.0, \\\"failure_rate\\\": 0.0, \\\"fixed_prompt_mse\\\": 0.0009485287964344025, \\\"full_budget_naive_mse\\\": 0.0009485287964344025, \\\"honest_half_mse\\\": 0.0019209212064743041, \\\"interval_width\\\": 0.16671460658773965, \\\"random_prompt_mse\\\": 0.0009485287964344025, \\\"report_bias\\\": 0.00018310546875, \\\"report_mse\\\": 0.0018619811534881592, \\\"reuse_mse\\\": 0.0019004708528518677, \\\"selected_accuracy\\\": 0.5, \\\"signed_optimism\\\": -0.0012836456298828125}.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"evidence_refs\": [\n        \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/solution/cases/2\",\n        \"analysis/condition_results.csv\",\nThis paper asks: \\emph{when does protected reporting reduce error after prompt selection, and what does an independent finite audit establish about that reduction?} We study a frozen bank with randomized half-split selection and reporting. The primary baseline reports the selection score of the \\emph{same} selected prompt. This isolates the reporting-data contrast from changes in the selected system. Additional baselines expose the cost of protection: full-budget selection and reuse, all-question fixed and random prompts, and an alternative half split.\n\nThe empirical contribution is deliberately bounded. Known-truth simulations separate selection optimism, reporting bias, squared error, and interval coverage. Real answer generation supplies a benchmark check, while an explicit distinction between finite-audit agreement and population accuracy prevents that check from being overinterpreted. The results show substantial improvements over same-winner reuse when selecting among sixteen prompts, but also clear counterexamples to universal error reduction. The study evaluates a conventional reporting design rather than proposing a new optimizer or a new post-selection guarantee.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n\n\\begin{figure}[t]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/reporting_overview.png}\n\\caption{Selection and reporting have different data roles. The protected and reuse reports describe the same selected prompt; full-budget selection can choose another prompt. Known truth supports population-error measurements in simulation, whereas a separate real-model audit supplies a noisy finite reference. Protection is an intended partition property, not a claim that every source of benchmark dependence has been eliminated.}\n\\label{fig:overview}\n\\end{figure}\n\nimport csv\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use('Agg')\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nplt.rcParams.update({'font.size': 9, 'axes.labelsize': 9, 'axes.titlesize': 9,\n                     'xtick.labelsize': 8.5, 'ytick.labelsize': 8.5,\n                     'legend.fontsize': 8.5, 'font.family': 'DejaVu Sans',\n                     'axes.spines.top': False, 'axes.spines.right': False,\n                     'pdf.fonttype': 42})\nCOLORS = ['#147D92', '#C45B26', '#635A9B']\nMETHODS = ['report_mse', 'reuse_mse', 'full_budget_naive_mse',\n           'honest_half_mse', 'fixed_prompt_mse', 'random_prompt_mse']\n\n\n\ndef manifest_entry(figure_id, figure_type, panels, rows, categories, series):\n    return {'figure_id': figure_id, 'figure_type': figure_type,\n            'path_pdf': f'figures/{figure_id}.pdf', 'path_png': f'figures/{figure_id}.png',\n            'generator': 'matplotlib', 'n_panels': panels, 'panels_per_row': rows,\n            'categories_per_panel': categories, 'series_per_panel': series,\n            'max_label_chars': 35, 'font_sizes': {'title': 9, 'axis': 9, 'ticks': 8.5, 'legend': 8.5},\n            'uses_abbrev_labels': True, 'uses_progression': False,\n            'placement': 'full_width', 'intended_latex_width_fraction': 1.0,\n            'estimated_min_rendered_font_pt': 8.5,\n            'source_ids': ['final.evidence.episodes']}\n\n\ndef main():\n    Path('figures').mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    Path('tables').mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    \"Ground quantitative claims in final.metric.* or final.evidence.episodes, qualification in final.qualification.*, and selection, search differences, and attempt accounting in study.*. Never substitute downstream_study.final_evaluation for the independent final record. If authoritative qualification changes to not_qualified, disclose it in the body, review, audit and revision; identify a cause only if evaluator evidence establishes it. The current source says qualified, not failed.\",\n    \"Private-only pipeline context: the retained search score equals its baseline score and has zero delta; these are not accuracy measurements or final-scope improvements. Do not put those internal score labels into visible figures. The baseline is the studied policy; do not manufacture a second identical baseline series.\",\n    \"Problem formalization should distinguish a prompt selected from a frozen bank, its conditional fresh-question accuracy, the reused selection mean, the protected report mean, and the finite audit estimate. Reporting MSE and selected-prompt accuracy answer different questions. Full-budget, fixed, random, and alternative-half methods have their own prompt targets, so their MSE differences do not isolate a single mechanism.\",\n    \"The real setting is HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-135M-Instruct revision 12fd25f77366fa6b3b4b768ec3050bf629380bac on MMLU-Pro revision b189ec765aa7ed75c8acfea42df31fdae71f97be, CPU float32, deterministic constrained one-letter generation. Do not replace it with an assumed 7B model, chain-of-thought optimizer, DSPy implementation, or free-form response task. Public-data pretraining contamination is possible, not established.\",\n    \"The four synthetic regimes cross equal/graded means and shared-outcome dependence; one prompt has no selection multiplicity. All source-defined conditions remain visible. The cross-family aggregate uses equal case/seed/regime weights rather than pooling synthetic replicates with real examples. Derive any display summaries reproducibly from paper_data.json and label weighting explicitly; do not introduce ungrounded numeric confidence intervals.\",\n    \"Observed control completion, zero replay discrepancy, and qualified status do not imply representative sampling, verified candidate diagnostics, adaptation-safe inference, or reliable repeated-population coverage. The copy-report control is deliberately contaminated and correctly records false independence. The decision-reversal metric uses protected-report-minus-full-sample-fixed versus selected-target-minus-fixed-target signs, excludes ties, and is not the probability that a naive claim is overturned; omit it from the main story unless its exact estimand is explained.\",\n    \"Use one common research question with separate evidential roles: known-truth simulation for bias/coverage and real inference for finite-audit agreement and prompt-accuracy uncertainty. Do not merge them into a single population coverage headline. Real audit pools overlap across settings and derive from a shared public pool; seed scatter is descriptive, not evidence for independent datasets or repeated training runs.\",\n    \"Body target is 8.5 pages within VENUE.md's 8-9-page limit, excluding references: 1.25 pages for title/abstract/problem/contributions and the early overview; 0.75 related work; 1.5 estimands and reporting policies; 1.0 design/provenance; 2.0 controlled comparisons with Figure 2 and the all-comparator table; 0.75 real audit uncertainty with Figure 3; 1.25 interpretation, limitations, reproducibility pointer and conclusion. These are layout allocations, not measured results. A body of exactly 8 pages requires its last page at least 75% full. Spend space on target distinctions, regime-wise uncertainty and counterexamples rather than larger figures, repeated prose or new experiments.\",\n    \"Suggested body headings: Introduction; Related Work; Selection and Reporting Targets; Reporting Policies; Experimental Design; Reporting Error and Selection Multiplicity; Finite-Audit Evidence; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion. Include a compact main table of all six comparators and a synthetic regime diagnostic table covering report bias, reuse optimism, coverage and interval width. The negative comparisons and finite-audit caveat remain in the body, not only the supplement.\",\n    \"Inspect and retain paper.sty's practical single-column geometry: 5.5 inches text width by 9 inches height. In this format column-width and full-width both span the one text column; the full_width figure designation means that span, not a two-column float. The local style has historical comments, and the staged task template is named iclr2027_conference while VENUE.md mandates ICLR 2026. Do not silently advertise the 2027 template as official 2026. Before final drafting/format validation, verify the required 2026 style provenance or obtain the exact official 2026 files through a direct known official source without prohibited-literature discovery; preserve anonymization and do not change geometry to force fit.\",\n    \"Place Supplementary Information after references in the same manuscript using clearpage, bibliography, clearpage, appendix, section Supplementary Information. Include the mandatory LLM Usage subsection, substantive full results and reproduction details. Route separately supplied appendix-ranked analyses there; do not guess or modify their ranking here.\",\n    \"Quantitative figures must be reproducible from local plotting source, exported as vector PDF and PNG at 300 DPI, with LaTeX referencing PDF whenever available. At full 5.5-inch span use at least 2400-pixel width for raster-only assets; any column inset uses at least 1200 pixels. Never upscale existing raster output. Retain editable concept-figure source and prompt provenance; at most one overview uses generate-concept-figure. Record final dimensions, placement and minimum rendered font in the later figure manifest.\",\n    \"References are a bibliography/provenance pool, not evidence that documents were read or that retrieved items are relevant. Do not pad related work with incidental retrieval matches. The permitted starter exact-title scope and retrieved Berk2013ValidPI provide positioning leads only after original-document consultation is verified; never invent missing MMLU-Pro, Wilson or bootstrap citations. Do not search for the forbidden paper, its identity, citation graph, summaries, or reproductions; stop and log any known accidental encounter. No external literature browsing was performed by this framing agent.\",\n    \"Do not claim paired certificates, outcome-dependent correction, quarter allocation, stratum-balanced gains, adaptive-search guarantees, unseen models, theoretical novelty, or completed ablations. Those are not measured interventions in the final evidence. No new inference, simulations, final paper, claim ledger, or final-paper validation belongs in this stage.\",\n    \"Ready means the artifacts support a bounded standalone strategy, not that they establish main-conference novelty, acceptance, statistical superiority, or completed reproduction. The template-year mismatch and precise citation consultation are explicit downstream production checks, not permission to dilute the scientific limitations.\"\n  ],\n  \"failure_reason\": \"\"\n}\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate generated claim-grounding artifacts before paper finalization.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport stat\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nKEY_RE = re.compile(r\"@\\w+\\{([^,]+),\")\nEVIDENCE_REF_RE = re.compile(r\"@evidence\\[\\[[^\\]]+\\]\\]\")\nTEX_INPUT_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?:input|include)(?![A-Za-z@])\\s*\"\n    r\"(?:\\{(?P<braced>[^{}]+)\\}|(?P<unbraced>[^\\s%{}]+))\"\n)\nTEX_IMPORT_COMMAND_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\(?:input|include)(?![A-Za-z@])\")\nTEX_LOCAL_SUPPORT_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?P<command>usepackage|RequirePackage|documentclass|LoadClass)\"\n    r\"(?![A-Za-z@])(?:\\s*\\[[^\\]]*\\])?\\s*\\{(?P<targets>[^{}]+)\\}\"\n)\nTEX_LOCAL_SUPPORT_COMMAND_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?:usepackage|RequirePackage|documentclass|LoadClass)(?![A-Za-z@])\"\n)\nDYNAMIC_TEX_IMPORT_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\csname\\s*(?:input|include)\\s*\\\\endcsname\")\nCONDITIONAL_TOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\if[a-zA-Z@]+\\b|\\\\else\\b|\\\\fi\\b\")\nVERBATIM_ENV_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\begin\\s*\\{(?P<env>verbatim\\*?|lstlisting|minted)\\}.*?\"\n    r\"\\\\end\\s*\\{(?P=env)\\}\",\n    re.DOTALL,\n)\nPROMPT_ARTIFACT_RE = re.compile(r\".+_prompt(?:_round_\\d+(?:_contract_retry_\\d+)?)?\\.md$\")\nGENERATED_EVIDENCE_SCAN_ARTIFACT_NAMES = {\n    \"validation_feedback.json\",\n{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"locator\": \"/final_evaluation\",\n      \"messages\": [\n        \"Target path exists, but locator semantics were not interpreted by the base verifier.\"\n      ],\n      \"raw_reference\": \"@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation]]\",\n      \"resolved_path\": \"paper_data.json\",\n      \"status\": \"anchored\",\n      \"subject_kind\": \"text-artifact\",\n      \"subject_path\": \"REPRODUCIBILITY.md\",\n      \"target\": \"paper_data.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"locator\": \"/downstream_study\",\n      \"messages\": [\n        \"Target path exists, but locator semantics were not interpreted by the base verifier.\"\n      ],\n      \"raw_reference\": \"@evidence[[paper_data.json#/downstream_study]]\",\n      \"resolved_path\": \"paper_data.json\",\n      \"status\": \"anchored\",\n      \"subject_kind\": \"text-artifact\",\n      \"subject_path\": \"REPRODUCIBILITY.md\",\n      \"target\": \"paper_data.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"locator\": \"/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\",\n      \"messages\": [\n        \"Target path exists, but locator semantics were not interpreted by the base verifier.\"\n      ],\n      \"raw_reference\": \"@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\",\n      \"resolved_path\": \"paper_data.json\",\n      \"status\": \"anchored\",\n      \"subject_kind\": \"text-artifact\",\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate rendered Supplementary Information in a compiled paper PDF.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef _letter_spaced_word_pattern(word: str) -> str:\n    return r\"[ \\t]*\".join(re.escape(character) for character in word)\n\n\nSUPPLEMENT_HEADING_RE = re.compile(\n    rf\"(?mi)^[ \\t]*(?:(?:appendix[ \\t]+)?[A-Z0-9]+(?:\\.\\d+)*[.:]?[ \\t]+)?\"\n    rf\"{_letter_spaced_word_pattern('supplementary')}[ \\t]+\"\n    rf\"{_letter_spaced_word_pattern('information')}[ \\t]*$\",\n)\nREFERENCE_HEADING_RE = re.compile(\n    rf\"(?mi)^[ \\t]*(?:{_letter_spaced_word_pattern('references')}|\"\n    rf\"{_letter_spaced_word_pattern('bibliography')})[ \\t]*$\"\n)\n\n\ndef parse_args() -> argparse.Namespace:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Validate rendered Supplementary Information in a PDF.\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"--pdf\", required=True)\n    return parser.parse_args()\n\n\ndef validate_rendered_supplementary_information(page_texts: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    supplement_page_index = next(\n        (\n            index\n            for index, page_text in enumerate(page_texts)\n            if SUPPLEMENT_HEADING_RE.search(page_text)\n        ),\n        None,\n    )\n    if supplement_page_index is None:\n        return [\"compiled paper is missing the Supplementary Information heading\"]\n\n    heading_page_text = page_texts[supplement_page_index]\n    heading_match = SUPPLEMENT_HEADING_RE.search(heading_page_text)\n    assert heading_match is not None\n    reference_page_indices = [\n        index\n        for index, page_text in enumerate(page_texts[:supplement_page_index])\n        if REFERENCE_HEADING_RE.search(page_text)\n    ]\n    errors: list[str] = []\n    if not reference_page_indices:\n        errors.append(\"compiled paper is missing the References heading before SI\")\n    heading_page_prefix = heading_page_text[: heading_match.start()]\n    prefix_lines = [line.strip() for line in heading_page_prefix.splitlines() if line.strip()]\n    earlier_header_lines = {\n        line.strip()\n        for page_text in page_texts[:supplement_page_index]\n        for line in page_text.splitlines()[:2]\n        if line.strip()\n    }\n    substantive_prefix_lines = [\n        line\n        for line in prefix_lines\n        if re.fullmatch(r\"(?:page\\s+)?\\d+\", line, re.IGNORECASE) is None\n        and line not in earlier_header_lines\n    ]\n    if substantive_prefix_lines:\n        errors.append(\n            \"compiled Supplementary Information must start on a separate page after References\"\n        )\n\n    supplement_chunks = [\n        heading_page_text[heading_match.end() :],\n        *page_texts[supplement_page_index + 1 :],\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
